    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d609">

                <pb facs="0724" n="714" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg714"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">103.9164: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-06">October 6,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received October 6—6 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8393. To Land, WSA, for Conway and Morse from Reed by Chubb. After consideration
                    of misgivings expressed in your 4047<anchor n="5" xml:id="d609-f1"/> we decided
                    to defer exploration of proposal as to time charters contained in Embassy
                        7790.<anchor n="5a" xml:id="d609-f2"/> Accordingly have not approached
                    Allies and will not raise matter until discussions following our return to
                    Washington. [Reed.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
